# Security Checks — Chave Project

Run this checklist at the end of every ticket before committing.

## Secrets & Environment Variables

**NEVER hardcode secrets, tokens, API keys, or phone numbers in source code.**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — never do this
const waNumber = '44999999999'
const apiKey = 'sk-abc123...'

// ✅ GOOD — always use environment variables
const waNumber = import.meta.env.VITE_WA_NUMBER
const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL
```

### .env Rules

- `.env.example` → commit with placeholder values only
- `.env`, `.env.production`, `.env.staging`, `.env.mock` → **never commit** (must be in `.gitignore`)
- `VITE_*` variables are exposed to the browser bundle — never put private keys or server secrets in them

### Before Every Commit — Scan for Secrets

```bash
# Check for common secret patterns accidentally staged
git diff --cached | grep -iE "(api_key|apikey|secret|password|token|Bearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9\-_]{20,}|sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,})"
```

If any match is found, **do not commit** — move the value to the appropriate `.env.*` file.

## Authentication

- JWT tokens must **never** be logged to console or sent to analytics
- Never log `email` + `password` together anywhere
- On HTTP 401 response → trigger automatic logout
- `autocomplete="current-password"` required on password fields (enables password managers)

## Client-Side Safety

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — XSS risk
element.innerHTML = userInput

// ✅ GOOD — safe
element.textContent = userInput
// or in React: just {userInput} (React escapes by default)
```

- Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless the content is explicitly sanitized
- External links must always have `rel="noopener noreferrer"` when `target="_blank"`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Link</a>
```

## End-of-Ticket Security Checklist

- [ ] No API keys, tokens, or phone numbers hardcoded in source files
- [ ] All secrets come from `import.meta.env.VITE_*`
- [ ] `.env` files with real values are NOT staged (`git status` check)
- [ ] No `console.log` with sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)
- [ ] External links have `rel="noopener noreferrer"`
- [ ] No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization
